        <div class="faq-a" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <div itemprop="text">
            <p>ELSS (Equity Linked Savings Scheme), accessible via SIP, is superior to Tax-Saver FDs for most investors. ELSS has a 3-year lock-in (vs 5 years for Tax-Saver FD), historical returns of 12–15% CAGR (vs 6.5–7.5% for FD), and the same ₹1.5 lakh deduction under Section 80C. The only advantage of a Tax-Saver FD is the guaranteed return — relevant if you cannot tolerate any market risk.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

